There are many cases where context (and/or common use) can be
unclear.  Many native English speakers incorrectly use the plural
"they" in lieu of the singular "he" when gender is unknown and "it"
would be contextually inappropriate or offensive.  It can be
confusing, even for a semi-native speaker such as myself.

A case could be made in favor of unique masculine, feminine,
indeterminate, and neuter pronouns for all three tenses.  24 (or more)
pronouns would make conversation more precise, although use of an
indeterminate/neuter "I" outside of a literary context would be ...
interesting.

